    {
      "title": "Adapter and Facade: Changing the Interface",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Adapter and Facade: Changing the Interface",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Adapter",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Client expects ==Target==; existing ==Adaptee== has an incompatible interface",
                "Adapter implements Target, **translates** each call to the Adaptee",
                "{green:Object adapter}: holds adaptee by composition, preferred, works with subclasses",
                "{orange:Class adapter}: inherits adaptee via multiple inheritance, rare"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "class XmlToJsonAdapter implements JsonSource {",
                "  constructor(private xml: XmlSource) {}",
                "  read() { return toJson(this.xml.read()); }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "object adapter: translates read()"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Facade",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One simplified entry point== over a complex subsystem",
                "`VideoConverter.convert(file, 'mp4')` hides codec, bitrate and audio classes",
                "Subsystem classes stay ==publicly usable=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Adapter vs Facade",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Adapter",
                "Facade"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Goal",
                  "Match an interface the client **already expects**",
                  "Define a **new, simpler** interface"
                ],
                [
                  "Wraps",
                  "One existing class",
                  "Many classes"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "God object",
              "text": "A Facade that grows ==business logic== becomes a god object. Keep it a thin delegator."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Decorator and Proxy: Same Interface, Different Intent",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Decorator and Proxy: Same Interface, Different Intent",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Decorator: add behaviour",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wraps an object with the ==same interface==, adds work before or after delegating",
                "Decorators ==stack==; the client picks the order",
                "Java: `new BufferedReader(new FileReader(f))`",
                "Python: `@decorator` adds logging or caching around a call"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "new Gzip(new Encrypt(new FileStream()))",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Gzip",
                    "note": "compress",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Encrypt",
                    "note": "then encrypt",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FileStream",
                    "note": "writes",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Proxy: control access",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stand-in with the ==same interface== that guards the real object",
                "{blue:Virtual}: lazy-load the costly object",
                "{green:Protection}: permission check",
                "{purple:Remote}: network stub",
                "{orange:Caching}: reuse earlier results"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Decorator vs Proxy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Decorator",
                "Proxy"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Purpose",
                  "Add features",
                  "Control access"
                ],
                [
                  "Chosen by",
                  "Client stacks it",
                  "Often invisible to client"
                ],
                [
                  "Real object",
                  "Passed in",
                  "Proxy manages lifecycle"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Order matters: compress then encrypt, since ciphertext barely compresses",
                "Proxy that swallows errors or breaks the interface",
                "Subclass per feature combination: class explosion, use decorators"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Quick test",
              "text": "Ask what the wrapper is for: **add** behaviour is Decorator, **guard** access is Proxy."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Composite and Bridge: Hierarchies and Abstractions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Composite and Bridge: Hierarchies and Abstractions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Composite: Tree as One Object",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Component== interface shared by **Leaf** and **Composite**",
                "Composite holds child Components, ==forwards calls==",
                "Client treats one object and a tree alike"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class File:",
                "    def size(self): return self.bytes",
                "class Folder:",
                "    def size(self):",
                "        return sum(c.size() for c in self.children)"
              ],
              "note": "Folder recurses; File is the base case"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`add()`, `remove()` on **Composite**: {green:safe}",
                "On **Component**: {blue:transparent}, leaves fail",
                "Trade-off: ==transparency vs safety=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Bridge: Two Dimensions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Abstraction== and ==Implementor== hierarchies joined by **composition**",
                "Shape with Renderer: Circle/Square x Vector/Raster",
                "==M+N== classes, not M×N"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Circle, Square",
                    "sub": "Abstraction",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Shape",
                    "sub": "holds a Renderer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vector, Raster",
                    "sub": "Implementor",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Bridge",
                "Adapter"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Built",
                  "Up front",
                  "After the fact"
                ],
                [
                  "Goal",
                  "Split two dimensions of change",
                  "Make incompatible classes fit"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Bridge when only **one** dimension varies",
                "Mixing up ==Strategy==: it swaps an algorithm, Bridge a whole implementation hierarchy"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
